#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""hub: one launcher for every game in the GameHub prefix (Steam, EA app, Ubisoft, Epic, standalone).

  hub list                       installed games, which launcher each needs, and how well it is known to work
  hub play <game> [options]      start the right launcher (if needed) and the game
  hub start <steam|ea|ubisoft>   start only a launcher
  hub status                     what is running in the prefix
  hub stop [game]                stop one game, or everything in the prefix (wineserver -k)
  hub trim epic                  stop the Epic launcher's processes while a game runs, to free memory (the game keeps running)
  hub doctor                     check volume, runtimes, prefix and launcher registrations

<game> is an alias (aoa, bf4, nfs, ...), a Steam app id, or any part of the name.
Options for play: --restart (stop what runs in the prefix first), --runtime NAME, --metalfx [FACTOR],
  --dxgi wined3d (AoA backend), --debug SPEC (WINEDEBUG), --no-wait, --force (known-blocked games),
  --keep-launcher (do not stop the Epic launcher 90 s after an Epic game started; see `hub trim`).

Layout (HUB_ROOT, default /Volumes/ExT2/GameHub): Prefix/ (one prefix), Runtimes/, Library/{Steam,Ubisoft,Epic}, "EA Games"/,
Hub/{Logs,State,Home,Temp}. This script and launcher/settings live in the repo; nothing else is needed from it on ExT2.
Only one Wine runtime can serve the prefix at a time (wineserver version mismatch), so switching between launchers
stops the launcher that is running.
"""
